<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/audio#AudioSignal> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An identified digital asset representing one or more channels of time-varying audio samples at a stated sample rate."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/audio#AudioSignal> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Frame coordinates apply only to a fixed signal identity or bitstream. Re-encoding, resampling, trimming, or channel changes create a distinct signal to which regions must be rebound."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/audio#LoopPointSet> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
